  "summary": "The leopard is recognized by its spotted coat. Jeremiah pictures it waiting outside cities, and Habakkuk uses its speed to describe the Chaldean horses. Isaiah pictures the same predator lying down with a young goat. Daniel and Revelation draw on its appearance in their descriptions of beasts.",
